      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Let me also check for the `EnumHeader` enum to understand the header values.Now I have a complete picture. Let me write the improved test with these understandability enhancements:\n- Remove all unused imports (`assertAll`, `assertArrayEquals`, etc.) and unused fields (`headerMap`, `record`)\n- Simplify `setUp()` to only create what the test actually uses\n- Replace `StringUtils.join` with standard `String.join` to drop the external dependency\n- Inline the `validateMap` helper (which was always called with `allowsNulls=true`), so the test reads as a flat sequence of clear assertions with no indirection\n- Tighten `throws Exception` to `throws IOException`Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored `CSVRecordTest_testToMap.java` removes all unused imports and fields, simplifies `setUp()` to only build `recordWithHeader`, replaces the `StringUtils.join` dependency with standard `String.join`, and inlines the `validateMap` helper into a flat, clearly-commented sequence of assertions — with no behavior change."
